Compute the existing movie window transform once per destination axis.

The native first-frame path spent about 23 ms before texture upload. The
existing filter repeats identical signed 64-bit divisions for every pixel.
Compute each column/row's unchanged fixed-point source index and 7-bit
fraction once. Preserve clipping, RepeatNone, weights, truncation, RGB565
quantization and opaque expansion exactly; do not fit clocks or images.

This reduces rendering latency without proving original/live A/V timing.

--- a/dd2_movie_surface.c
+++ b/dd2_movie_surface.c
